caption: Preserved Requirements

This pass standardizes the numerical Mastery dimensions named here and in the Engine-specific standards below. Do not infer additional numerical gates beyond those standards. Tier 1 Mastery remains intentionally variable. Breadth counts such as the number of abilities, categories, forms, or authored works, including Tier 3 authorship counts, remain Engine- or Tradition-specific unless separately ruled. Pet and Commander remain pending until those Engines have functional chassis. Regular, Ritual, Inspired, Realm, and Word use their Engine-specific progression instead of a separate point-investment floor. Realm requires the Tradition's Realms themselves to be purchased to maximum; Word uses its lexicon, skill, and any actual Word-purchase requirements. Enhancement uses its generation-and-sharing totals in place of the Tier 3 point-investment floor. Preserve every nonnumerical requirement: spell or skill breadth, mastered techniques, required purchases or stages, consequential use, deeds, authorship, teaching, and other Engine-specific demonstrations. Experience earned or generated, an ability's capacity, and equipment or project costs are not a character-point investment requirement unless the Engine-specific standard explicitly says so.
